course: dictionary
lesson: 1083
title: Words for a time of life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Boyhood is the time in a person's life when he is a boy. It starts at birth and lasts until he becomes a young man. The ending -hood is a clue: it turns a word into a name for a time or state, as in childhood.
explain: «Their best fighters were knights, rich horsemen trained from boyhood, who wore heavy armour and painted coats of arms on their shields so friends could tell who was who in battle.» The words trained from boyhood tell you the knights started their training as boys, long before they were grown men. Read the words around boyhood and the meaning follows.
explain: Writers use boyhood when they tell the story of a famous person's early years, such as his boyhood home, his boyhood dream or his boyhood friend. To check the meaning, swap in a simpler phrase, like "when he was a boy", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Boyhood means the time in a person's life when he is a boy, from birth until he becomes a young man.
fact: Boyhood can also mean the state of being a boy.
fact: The ending -hood means a time or state, as in childhood and boyhood.
fact: Boyhood is usually said as "his boyhood" or "in boyhood", not "a boyhood" or "two boyhoods".
fact: Useful phrases: «boyhood home», «boyhood dream», «boyhood friend».
exercise: «Knights were trained from boyhood.» When did their training start? | When they were grown men | At the end of a battle | *When they were boys | After they had retired
exercise: Which word means the time when a person is a boy? | Fatherhood | *Boyhood | Manhood
exercise: «His boyhood dream was to fly.» What does boyhood dream mean? | A dream he had when he was old | A dream about a boy in a film | *A dream he had when he was a boy
test: «Her boyhood home was by the sea.» What does boyhood home mean? | A home for boys only at school | The home she bought when she was old | *The home where she grew up as a child
test: He spent his ___ in a small village by the sea. Which word fits best? | Bravery | *boyhood | Silence
exam: What does the -hood in boyhood tell us? | *It shows a time or state, like childhood | It means a place to live | It means the word is an animal | It means the word is a colour
